ct that leans Republican by about five points. She faces state Representative Derek Merrin, who has raised a credible $1.5 million but trails Kaptur's $4.3 million war chest by a wide margin. Expert ratings split between Tossup and Lean D, with Inside Elections the lone outlier at Tilt R.\n\nThe only recent poll, from the DCCC's own shop, showed the race tied at 48-48, and Republican-sponsored spring polls had Merrin slightly ahead. Prediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket price Kaptur's win chances near 70%. Trans-issue attacks have drawn attention from both directions, but the race remains close, with Kaptur holding a slight edge on incumbency and money in a tough environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7474, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7282, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7313, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7108, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6729, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6764, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7175, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7321, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7015, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7133, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7126, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6869, "margin": 2.5}]}